# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# master -- the PUBLIC branch.
#
# It tracks only the shipped library, the runnable examples, the test suite, the
# frozen V3 model artifacts and packaging. Working material (doc/, archive/,
# notebooks/, slides/, agent instruction files) is tracked on the `dev` branch.
#
# This branch has its OWN history, unrelated to dev's, so that publishing it does
# not expose the internal working history. Do not merge between the two branches
# in either direction. Publish with:
#     git checkout dev -- sbs_shear examples tests models README.md pyproject.toml
# See doc/BRANCHES.md on the dev branch.
#
# This is a WHITELIST: every top-level entry is ignored, then the public tree is
# re-admitted below. To publish a new top-level directory, add a `!` line for it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/*

!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/pyproject.toml
!/sbs_shear/
!/examples/
!/tests/
!/models/

# ---- caches and build junk, anywhere in the public tree ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---- editor / agent scratch ----
*.orig
*.swp
*.rblendbak
*.swabak
*.stale_bak
